WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.371
What happens when the flight computer itself freezes?

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:07.626
If the failsafe is software, it freezes too.

00:00:07.626 --> 00:00:10.067
D100 puts the rescue in hardware.

00:00:11.117 --> 00:00:19.629
Inertial sensors and the radio link reach two flight cores, one flying the drone and one navigating, in hard real time.

00:00:20.679 --> 00:00:29.724
Cameras feed a pose engine made of geometry rather than a trained network, so it keeps working with no satellite signal at all.

00:00:30.774 --> 00:00:38.753
Camera features and inertial data fuse into a full pose, 30 times a second, delivered straight to the flight loop.

00:00:39.803 --> 00:00:45.512
In normal flight, the motor commands leave on eight channels to the speed controllers.

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:48.699
That path trusts the flight cores to be running.

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:54.748
The failsafe island runs on its own power and its own clock.

00:00:54.748 --> 00:01:02.162
It notices a lost link, lost GPS or a sensor fault in hardware, and picks return or land.

00:01:03.212 --> 00:01:08.237
Then it drives the speed controllers directly, without the flight computer.

00:01:08.237 --> 00:01:10.984
This is a structure, not a proven result.

00:01:12.034 --> 00:01:15.539
No D100 silicon has been made or measured.

00:01:15.539 --> 00:01:20.463
An FPGA validates the design, and every figure is a target.

00:01:20.463 --> 00:01:24.218
Bring us your mission and your failure cases.

00:01:24.218 --> 00:01:27.389
We will tell you what D100 must prove.
